A||||38||mrfiero||Unbelieveable!||||4||
Z||000000||mrfiero||10-10-2000||01:33 PM||||Yesterday afternoon, while going to retrieve the '86 SE I just bought, I spotted a silver fastback on a dealer lot.  I went back later to look at it and discovered it was an '88 GT!  Being fond of '88 GT's I asked what they were asking for it, the kid said $3488.  I thought to myself that this was a good price considering it only had 65K miles.  <P>I made an offer of $2500 and yada, yada, yada we finally agreed on a price of $3200 out the door.  I left a $500 deposit and said I'll pay the $2700 balance off when I pick it up next week.  We filled out all of the paperwork and I was off.          <P><BR>This morning I wake up with a message on my machine from the salesman who sold it to me (it's a buy here, pay here lot, BTW).  I called him and he said his "boss" had chewed him out for selling it to me so low....he claimed that their "cash valuation" was higher than the $3200 I paid for it.  They want to give me my $500 back and forget the whole deal!  <P>I asked the guy what if the roles were reversed?  Would the dealer be willing to refund my money?  I don't think so!<P>I don't want to be an a$$hole here, but as far as I'm concerned we have a legally binding agreement for $3200.  <P>What are you're opinions?   ||||reg||4
Z||000001||deceler8||10-10-2000||01:52 PM||||You have a legal, binding contract. <P>Tell the guy you're going to report him to the consumer affairs division of your states' attorney general office if he doesn't follow through.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-10-2000||01:53 PM||||i agree with you.. you signed the papers.. if HIS boss is mad thats NOT your problem that the salesmans problem! COngrats! you just won an 88 GT! sweet score  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||10-10-2000||02:48 PM||||<BR>Let's get this straight. They dropped the price a <I>whole</I> <B>$288</B> from the original asking price of $3488 and now they're saying that they sold it for too low a price. Screw them. Sounds to me like someone walked into the lot and offered more money AFTER they had already accepted your offer. Don't let these sleazebags con you.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-10-2000||02:50 PM||||The $3200 included tax and D&H.  The actual price of the car was $2750.<P>Thanks for everyones input.  I will be holding them to the contract.....hopefully this doesn't get ugly.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||10-10-2000||03:01 PM||||I am not sure if his applies to your state but, A friend went to purchase a minivan and worked out a deal with the salesman to pick up the car the next night. When he returned the dealership claimed that the sale price he paid was below what they gave for a trade-in and wanted more money or to refund his deposit. He asked to borrow the phone and called his Bother-in-law who was a lawyer.<BR>If you have a sales receipt with the salesmans signature stating how much he sold the car for he has to abide by it or you can go to court and get the vehicle or the total cost of the vehicle given to you! Read: You could get the car for free! Besides I thought the salesman had to get all deals approved by the sales manager before signing?<BR>It does sound like someone else offered more money for it and they are being greedy f**ks.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||wkayl||10-10-2000||03:01 PM||||Call Tom Martino!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||10-10-2000||03:09 PM||||call johnny cochrain!||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||10-10-2000||03:16 PM||||There were actually 3 people involved in this sale.....the salesman, the sales "manager" and the lady who typed up the contract.   So you are correct Oreif.....the guy who approved of the negotiations should have known then and there if the price was too low or not.  I sent the salesman back to him with 3 different offers, so they had plenty of time to figure it all out.<P>I suspect that they either had a higher offer or the $3488 price was supposed to be higher.  Either way, my hands are clean and the car should be mine.<P>If I had paid the entire $3200 yesterday and drove it home, we wouldn't be having this conversation, so they're just SOL (s#it outta luck!)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><BR>wkayl,<P>If they try to renig on the deal I'm definitley giving Tom a call! <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||10-10-2000||04:01 PM||||Mike,<P>My last employer was a car dealership here in Ohio.  I could happily call the used car mgr. and see what he has to say about the situation.  <P>As far as I know, the car is yours at the agreed upon price.  Dealers can be rather shitty though.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000010||bHooper||10-10-2000||04:32 PM||||it definately sounds as if somone came in behind you and offered them more money for the car.  <P>but a contract is a contract, and cannot be broken unless both parties come to an agreement!<P>the car is yours!  go and pick it up!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||10-10-2000||05:10 PM||||I agree with Patrick. Someone offered him more money for it. Geat deal!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierosound||10-10-2000||07:58 PM||||Great deal.  I'd be there with a cheque and a lawyer to pick up that car right away, before they have a change to mess with the car.  If it gets ugly, you may end up getting the car with slight damage of the "you just didn't notice it before" type.  The only thing going through their minds seems to be $$$, and who knows what they'd do it they felt you "cheated them".||||reg||10
Z||000013||mrfiero||10-10-2000||08:50 PM||||Thanks for all of your input!  I indeed have a binding contract....I have the bill of sale and all of the other pertinent paperwork in my hand, so they have no choice but to honor the agreement.  I will have my lawyer standing by, just in case though.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm trying to round up the rest of the cash as we speak so I can pick it up ASAP.<P>I figure it'll be better for me to show up with the cash in hand and pick it up instead of calling them to say I'm keeping it and will pick it up in a week.  As some of you have mentioned....some "damage" may occur to it in the meantime.<P><BR>Thanks again.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||10
