Z||000017||Mattsfiero||10-11-2000||07:49 AM||||Okay I see the point here. Yes the contract is a legal binding one. The man needs to cut his loss and get over it. I will also say that here I don't know about there , There is a law that states that any Vehicle sold for more than $599 must pass inspection unless sold as is or for parts wich must be stated on the contract or Bill of sale this is called "The Lemon Law". if he damages the car in any way he is responsible for the repairs for up to 30 days and responsible for it to pass the state inspection as well. Check and see if the same laws apply to you there. Oh and that is an awsome find By the way!!!<P>Good luck with it||||reg||4
Z||000018||stsmithgt||10-11-2000||01:16 PM||||If you have a cell phone or borrow one just in case they try to keep the car, you can call the sheriff while keeping gaurd over YOUR car.  Expect to make a day of it. you know, "expect the worst and hope for the best!" Oh yeah, make sure you have an assortment of phone numbers on hand to help claim your prize.  I like that get your car free from the judge thing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000019||Patrick||10-11-2000||05:46 PM||||<BR>tick, tick, tick...<P>The suspense is unbearable! <P>I wanna know what happened! I wanna go for a ride!||||reg||10
Z||000020||mrfiero||10-11-2000||06:32 PM||||This thing has gotten  really ugly.  I just came from the dealership....I was attempting to pay the balance and take the car, but they refused!  I can't give the specifics right now, but listen to Tom Martino--"the trouble shooter" tomorrow.  He is a nationally syndicated consumer rights fighter (or whatever).  He's based here in Denver, but has a national radio program.  I called them today and was told to give them a call tomorrow at 11:50 am (mountain time)......I'm assuming the show is broadcast at noon here, but I'm not sure.  <P>I have to get ahold of the dealer licensing board first, but they don't seem willing to answer their phone.  <P>Without delving too much into it right now (it'll all come out tomorrow) they are trying to renig on this deal through a technicality.  I'm assuming they mistakenly sold it to me at a lower price than they wanted and are now trying to bar me from taking delivery of it because of one little thing.  <P>It really ticks me off!  <P>Tune in to Tom Martino tomorrow.....hopefully I'll be on the air and something will get done!        ||||reg||8
Z||000021||Old Lar||10-11-2000||08:00 PM||||Go get em, Mike.  I had a run around from a dealer years ago(1982).  He wanted to hold onto my deposit money after he couldn't deliver a car that I ordered.  I had leased the car Chrysler sent for me, which didn't have the engine option I ordered, while waiting for the reorder to come in.  That came in with the wrong interior.  He cried he lost money on the lease.  I had to file a complaint with the local automobile dealers association (he was the president at the time).  I did get a complete refund, but he jerked me around for six months.  I got no support from Chrysler Corp at all.  I have never considered a Chrsler car since nor a Chrysler dealer for a car purchase.  Give em he11.||||reg||14
Z||000022||fiero56||10-11-2000||09:56 PM||||Mike,<BR>Just make sure you have registration and insurance on this car before you go driving cross-country <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. You don't want a repeat do you???<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||wkayl||10-11-2000||10:48 PM||||For those of you who don't have "Tom Martino the Troubleshooter" in their radio marked, he is broadcast on the web.  Here is the link<BR> <A HREF="http://www.khow.com/home.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.khow.com/home.html</A> <P>To view his web-site, here is the link to it<BR> <A HREF="http://www.troubleshooter.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.troubleshooter.com/</A> <P>I have edited this post to include the times of his show.  12:00PM to 3:00PM mountain.  He also takes live e-mail on his show and comments on it from time to time.<P>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 10-11-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||mrfiero||10-11-2000||11:18 PM||||Fiero56,<P>It's because of that little incident that is causing my problems.  It'll all come out tomorrow if I am indeed on the radio program.  I guess making an a$$ out of myself will be worth it if I do wind up getting this GT.  I have my doubts & reservations about this.....I have a nasty feeling I'll lose.  I guess I shouldn't jinx myself......I'll know tomorrow what'll happen. <P>Sorry about being so vague right now.....I just don't want to publicize my persoanl problems if I don't have to.  It may come out on the radio, if I am aired, so I'll have to deal with that if/when it happens.<P>I guess that explaination was just as vague....sorry.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000025||mrfiero||10-12-2000||02:25 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">YES!YES!YES!YES!YES!YES!YES!YES!YES! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I just got off the phone with the Colorado Dealers licensing Division and the dealership.......the loophole that they tried to use to get out of the deal doesn't exist, so I am on my way to pick up the GT!!!<P>I did all of this without calling Tom Martino back.....I sort of wish I had gotten on the show so I could have bad mouthed their dealership a bit, but I can't complain.....I got a 65K mile '88 GT for $3200!!||||reg||14
