Z||000030||mrfiero||10-12-2000||07:29 PM||||I picked it up this afternoon without incident from the dealer.  He says the salesman will get docked $1500, but I seriously doubt that.  They claim that the original asking price was $7988 and that the salesman screwed up by saying $3488.  Evidently they had $3000 into it as a trade, so I bought it for less than they had into it (I paid $2750 + taxes).<P>Oh well for them!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm certainly not going to lose sleep over a dealership losing money on a sale!  In fact, it's about time.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Thanks for everyone's input.....I really wanted to run their name through the mud too, but a peaceful ending is just as good.<P>I will post pictures of all of my Fieros as soon as I can (I really need to break down and buy a digital camera!).   ||||reg||10
Z||000031||Cliff Pennock||10-12-2000||08:18 PM||||Congrats!<P>I wouldn't worry about the dealer loosing any money 'cos they don't. If they <B>really</B> wanted to get out of that contract, they not only would have offered you your deposit back, but some extra money as well. If the salesman needs to pay back the $1500, I'm sure he would have offered you at least an extra $500 to get out of the deal. Simple math. He just wants to make you feel guilty. ||||reg||14
